\begin{equation*} b_{g} = \frac{\sum _d n_{g,d}}{\sum _d \sum _g n_{g,d}}, \end{equation*}\end{document}where ng, d is the number of counts for gene g in droplet d and the sum over d is taken over all droplets with <Nemp UMIs (Fig. 1). The species-mixing experiment allows us to compare how accurately bg recapitulates the true background expression found within each cell, revealing that any value of Nemp < 100 produces a good correlation, with the best correlation given when Nemp < 10 (Supplementary Fig. S2).", "locator": {"kind": "section", "value": "source-artifact:c077c1f8c4f5ca49b8a82f25e0fae735/xml:/article/body/sec[2]/p[4];text-sha256:777cf343f0167f7547104c764e4a8c31f33e77873c2b44c21032cb08ff973fef:3764:4722"}, "ontology_version": "2.0.0-core-review.1", "schema_version": "sckg-ontology-core-5c-design-v1", "section": "xml:/article/body/sec[2]/p[4]", "source_artifact_id": "source-artifact:c077c1f8c4f5ca49b8a82f25e0fae735", "source_revision_id": "source-revision:9c88c5d94c9742da426d218b", "start_offset": 3764}], "execution_authorized": false, "human_review_status": "pending", "routing_basis": "Source co-occurrence or explicit gap subject; not an ontology relation or applicability assertion.", "scope_status": "unknown", "source_excerpt_available": true, "status": "unasserted_candidate_caution", "subject_ids": ["method:soupx", "method:soupx-marker-contamination-estimation"], "supports_negative_claim": false, "supports_positive_claim": false, "scientific_assertion": false, "trusted": false, "production_retrieval_eligible": false, "execution_gate": false}, {"caution_id": "evidence-gap:cab33c88e969fce65b4fb8a4", "description": "Manual contamination fraction alternative: Manual setting remains an alternative; no blanket requirement for automated estimation or marker availability.", "evidence": [{"content_hash": "fa1faf759c9fff702991c7c31cfd33bde0600c7fe2d4113564f3e407c26718ac", "end_offset": 30934, "evidence_span_id": "evidence-span:b652da458b4e94d49ebf863e", "exact_text": "It is also possible to manually specify the contamination fraction, which can be useful when the aforementioned estimation procedures are deemed inaccurate or it is desirable to overcorrect the data. For most applications, the consequences of manually setting an unrealistically high contamination rate are likely to be minimal. Contamination is preferentially removed from genes closest to the background expression (i.e., genes with low levels of expression), meaning that setting a higher global contamination rate is unlikely to completely remove the expression of genes that are truly markers of a cell. Thus in some applications it may be preferable to overcorrect for background contamination and remove a small amount of genuine signal to ensure that all the background contamination has been removed. We also find that our method is robust to small inaccuracies in the estimation of the global contamination rate (Supplementary Fig. S4).", "locator": {"kind": "section", "value": "source-artifact:c077c1f8c4f5ca49b8a82f25e0fae735/xml:/article/body/sec[6]/p[6];text-sha256:777cf343f0167f7547104c764e4a8c31f33e77873c2b44c21032cb08ff973fef:29988:30934"}, "ontology_version": "2.0.0-core-review.1", "schema_version": "sckg-ontology-core-5c-design-v1", "section": "xml:/article/body/sec[6]/p[6]", "source_artifact_id": "source-artifact:c077c1f8c4f5ca49b8a82f25e0fae735", "source_revision_id": "source-revision:9c88c5d94c9742da426d218b", "start_offset": 29988}], "execution_authorized": false, "human_review_status": "pending", "routing_basis": "Source co-occurrence or explicit gap subject; not an ontology relation or applicability assertion.", "scope_status": "unknown", "source_excerpt_available": true, "status": "unasserted_candidate_caution", "subject_ids": ["method:soupx", "method:soupx-marker-contamination-estimation"], "supports_negative_claim": false, "supports_positive_claim": false, "scientific_assertion": false, "trusted": false, "production_retrieval_eligible": false, "exe